## Why This Is Asked
This question probes the candidate's ability to reason with Kleene three-valued logic, construct concrete model assignments, and outline an efficient backtracking/projection strategy under uncertain information.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene three-valued semantics and implications
- Constraint propagation under partial information
- Backtracking with early pruning in a small search space

## Code Example
```javascript
const F=0, U=1, T=2;
function not(x){ return x===T?F: x===F?T:U; }
function and(a,b){ return Math.min(a,b); }
function or(a,b){ return Math.max(a,b); }
function implies(a,b){ return or(not(a), b); }

// assignment: G1=T, G2=U, G3=U, G4=T, G5=U
const G1=T, G2=U, G3=U, G4=T, G5=U;
const c1 = implies(G1,G2);
const c2 = or(not(G3), G4);
const c3 = implies(and(G2,G5), not(G1));
const c4 = implies(or(G4,G5), G3);
const c5 = or(and(G1, not(G5)), and(not(G1), G5));
// c1..c5 are all non-F in this example
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this to n guards and a mix of 2-valued and 3-valued constraints?
- How does short-circuit evaluation affect pruning in a real solver?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests extending Boolean logic to 3-valued systems with biconditionals in realistic feature-flag scenarios, plus constraint propagation and backtracking techniques.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene 3-valued logic for →, ∧, ∨ operations
- Biconditional as (A→B) ∧ (B→A)
- Constraint propagation with Unknown handling and backtracking
- Feature-flag rollout scenarios with partial information

## Code Example
```javascript
// Kleene values: F < U < T
const rank = {F:0, U:1, T:2};
function not(v){ return v==='T'?'F': v==='F'?'T':'U'; }
function implies(a,b){ const na = not(a); return [na, b].reduce((x,y)=>rank[x]>=rank[y]?x:y); }
function and(a,b){ return [a, b].reduce((x,y)=>rank[x]<=rank[y]?x:y); }
function or(a,b){ return [a, b].reduce((x,y)=>rank[x]>=rank[y]?x:y); }
```

## Approach
The propagation algorithm iteratively applies constraints, treating U as flexible until forced to T or F. When conflicts arise, it backtracks systematically through the remaining U values.

## Why This Is Asked
Tests reasoning with Kleene 3-valued logic, construct a satisfying assignment with U present, and perform constrained backtracking. 

## Key Concepts
Kleene semantics; implication as ¬X ∨ Y; propagation; small depth search.

## Code Example
